Let’s deep dive and see where and why to use @Transactional in your current TaskService methods.

💡 First, Recap: What @Transactional Really Does
Begins a DB transaction

If method finishes successfully → ✅ Commit

If any runtime exception → ❌ Rollback automatically

Ensures data consistency and atomicity

🧾 Your Service Methods:
java
Copy
Edit
String createTask(TaskDto taskDto);
