This version does NOT support readOnly = true.

✅ Use the correct one:
java
Copy
Edit
// ✅ CORRECT
import org.springframework.transaction.annotation.Transactional;
Only Spring’s version supports all attributes like readOnly, rollbackFor, propagation, etc.

🔍 How to check and fix in IntelliJ:
Place cursor on @Transactional → Ctrl+Click

It should go to org.springframework.transaction.annotation.Transactional

If not, remove wrong import and add the correct one manually

✅ Final Correct Example:
java
Copy
Edit
import org.springframework.transaction.annotation.Transactional;

@Transactional(readOnly = true)
public List<TaskDto> getAllTask() {
    return repo.findAll().stream()... // etc
}
🧠 Summary:
Attribute	jakarta.transaction	springframework.transaction
readOnly = true	❌ Not supported	✅ Supported
rollbackFor	❌ Not supported	✅ Supported
propagation	❌ Not supported	✅ Supported

💬 Final Interview Tip:
“We use @Transactional(readOnly = true) from Spring to optimize read-only service methods and avoid unnecessary persistence context overhead.”

